The paper introduces a view of differential privacy that is linked to the literature on measurement error models, which allows for some fruitful exchange of ideas.

Strengths: simplicity of idea; the connection described appears sounds and can suggest new ideas to be pursued;

Weaknesses: there were a variety of concerns regarding soundness and applicability (both as is and in more general setups).
